ReadBoot Branding Standards ("Futurist Carton")
1. Visual Identity
Aesthetic: High-contrast, editorial cartoon style with thick linework.

Linework: Use consistent 4px solid charcoal borders ($ref-color-charcoal) for all primary containers and buttons.

Corner Radius: Use 12px rounded corners to mimic hand-drawn ink art.

2. Design Tokens (Source of Truth)
Always use tokens from `packages/ui/src/patterns/Atoms/**` token modules instead of hardcoded values:

Colors:

Paper Background: $sys-color-paper-bg (#FAF9F6)

Ink/Text: $sys-color-ink-text (#36454F)

Action Primary: $sys-color-action-primary (#DC143C)

Typography:

Headlines: Baloo 2 (Weight: 700).

Body: Inter (Academic/Clean).

3. Interactive Effects & Layout
Hover States: Interactive elements must feel "bouncy." Use a 1.05 scale transform with a bouncy cubic-bezier easing.

Grid Layout: For long-form text, implement newspaper-inspired column layouts using CSS column-count.

Note: "The Glitch" effect is officially deprecated and has been removed from the system. Do NOT apply .fx--glitch.

4. Technical Requirements
Format: Use SCSS Modules (.module.scss) exclusively. No CSS-in-JS or Styled-Components.

SCSS Modules: Prefer local `@use` imports from token modules under `packages/ui/src/patterns/Atoms/**` in component `.module.scss` files.

5. Newspaper layout vocabulary
**Full glossary and when to use each term:** **`readboot-newspaper-terminology.mdc`** (boxed vs full-bleed, kicker, deck, lead, rule, etc.). Prefer that vocabulary in docs, Storybook descriptions, and SCSS comments; component **code names** stay per `ui-atomic-architecture.mdc`.

**Hero shorthand:** **Boxed feature** = component `BoxedFeatureHero` (ruled shell). **Full-bleed / open** = component `FullBleedHero` (portrait + lead on newsprint, no outer rule on the band). In CSS Modules, encode with local roots like `.rootBoxed` / `.rootBleed` or `data-layout`, not loose global BEM unless one root wraps the block.
